  "brief": "Small one-storey Folk Victorian farm cottage of 1878: a hipped roof with a steep centered front cross gable carrying a little spindled gable truss and a louvered attic vent, white weatherboard walls with plain corner boards and flat-headed tall one-over-one windows. The centered front door has only a concrete stoop and a tiny striped metal awning; a TV antenna mast stands on the roof. Low round shrubs flank the steps, large old shade trees close around it, lawn in front.",
